### What are gRPC status codes?

Every gRPC call ends with a status, which is a numeric code plus an optional message, sent in the HTTP/2 trailer. Each code has a precise meaning that drives client behavior.

| Code | Name | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| 0 | OK | Success |
| 1 | CANCELLED | Caller cancelled the call |
| 3 | INVALID_ARGUMENT | Client sent a bad value |
| 4 | DEADLINE_EXCEEDED | Call ran past its deadline |
| 5 | NOT_FOUND | Entity does not exist |
| 6 | ALREADY_EXISTS | Create conflicts with existing entity |
| 7 | PERMISSION_DENIED | Authenticated but not authorized |
| 12 | UNIMPLEMENTED | Method not implemented |
| 13 | INTERNAL | Server bug |
| 14 | UNAVAILABLE | Transient outage, retryable |
| 16 | UNAUTHENTICATED | No valid identity |

```java
package com.bank.grpc;

import io.grpc.Status;
import io.grpc.stub.StreamObserver;

public class AccountGrpcService
        extends AccountServiceGrpc.AccountServiceImplBase {

    @Override
    public void getBalance(
            BalanceRequest request,
            StreamObserver<BalanceResponse> observer) {

        String accountId = request.getAccountId();
        if (accountId == null || accountId.isBlank()) {
            observer.onError(
                Status.INVALID_ARGUMENT
                    .withDescription("Account ID must not be empty")
                    .asRuntimeException()
            );
            return;
        }

        Account account = findAccount(accountId);
        if (account == null) {
            observer.onError(
                Status.NOT_FOUND
                    .withDescription("Account " + accountId
                        + " not found")
                    .asRuntimeException()
            );
            return;
        }

        observer.onNext(BalanceResponse.newBuilder()
                .setBalance(account.getBalance().toPlainString())
                .build());
        observer.onCompleted();
    }
}
```

### Why does choosing the right code matter for retries?

The status code drives client retry behavior. UNAVAILABLE and sometimes DEADLINE_EXCEEDED are safe to retry because the failure is transient. INVALID_ARGUMENT and NOT_FOUND must not be retried because they will always fail the same way.

```java
package com.bank.grpc;

import io.grpc.Status;
import io.grpc.StatusRuntimeException;
import java.math.BigDecimal;

public class TransferClient {

    public BigDecimal transferWithRetry(
            String from, String to, String amount) {
        int maxRetries = 3;
        for (int i = 0; i < maxRetries; i++) {
            try {
                return doTransfer(from, to, amount);
            } catch (StatusRuntimeException e) {
                Status.Code code = e.getStatus().getCode();
                if (code == Status.Code.UNAVAILABLE) {
                    System.out.println("Retry " + (i + 1)
                        + ": service unavailable");
                    continue; // Safe to retry
                }
                if (code == Status.Code.INVALID_ARGUMENT) {
                    throw e; // Do NOT retry
                }
                throw e; // Unknown, do not retry
            }
        }
        throw new RuntimeException("Transfer failed after retries");
    }

    private BigDecimal doTransfer(
            String from, String to, String amount) {
        // Stub call
        return new BigDecimal("50000.00");
    }
}
```

### How do gRPC codes map to HTTP codes in gateways?

When a gRPC-Web or REST gateway sits in front, it maps gRPC codes to HTTP status codes.

| gRPC Code | HTTP Status |
|---|---|
| OK (0) | 200 |
| INVALID_ARGUMENT (3) | 400 |
| UNAUTHENTICATED (16) | 401 |
| PERMISSION_DENIED (7) | 403 |
| NOT_FOUND (5) | 404 |
| ALREADY_EXISTS (6) | 409 |
| RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED (8) | 429 |
| INTERNAL (13) | 500 |
| UNIMPLEMENTED (12) | 501 |
| UNAVAILABLE (14) | 503 |

### How do you return rich error details?

The richer error model packs a `google.rpc.Status` message into the trailer. It carries the code, a message, and a list of typed detail messages. Standard detail types include `ErrorInfo`, `BadRequest`, and `RetryInfo`.

```java
package com.bank.grpc;

import com.google.protobuf.Any;
import com.google.rpc.BadRequest;
import com.google.rpc.ErrorInfo;
import io.grpc.protobuf.StatusProto;
import io.grpc.stub.StreamObserver;
import java.math.BigDecimal;

public class TransferGrpcService
        extends TransferServiceGrpc.TransferServiceImplBase {

    @Override
    public void transfer(
            TransferRequest request,
            StreamObserver<TransferResponse> observer) {

        BigDecimal amount = new BigDecimal(request.getAmount());

        if (amount.compareTo(BigDecimal.ZERO) <= 0) {
            // Rich error with BadRequest field violation
            BadRequest badRequest = BadRequest.newBuilder()
                .addFieldViolations(
                    BadRequest.FieldViolation.newBuilder()
                        .setField("amount")
                        .setDescription(
                            "Amount must be positive, got: "
                            + amount.toPlainString())
                        .build()
                ).build();

            com.google.rpc.Status status =
                com.google.rpc.Status.newBuilder()
                    .setCode(com.google.rpc.Code.INVALID_ARGUMENT_VALUE)
                    .setMessage("Invalid transfer request")
                    .addDetails(Any.pack(badRequest))
                    .build();

            observer.onError(
                StatusProto.toStatusRuntimeException(status));
            return;
        }

        // Process transfer...
        observer.onNext(TransferResponse.newBuilder()
                .setSuccess(true).build());
        observer.onCompleted();
    }
}
```

### How does the client parse rich error details?

The client extracts detail messages from the exception using `StatusProto.fromThrowable()`.

```java
package com.bank.client;

import com.google.rpc.BadRequest;
import io.grpc.StatusRuntimeException;
import io.grpc.protobuf.StatusProto;

public class TransferErrorHandler {

    public void handleError(StatusRuntimeException e) {
        com.google.rpc.Status status =
            StatusProto.fromThrowable(e);

        if (status != null) {
            System.out.println("Code: " + status.getCode());
            System.out.println("Message: " + status.getMessage());

            for (com.google.protobuf.Any detail
                    : status.getDetailsList()) {
                if (detail.is(BadRequest.class)) {
                    try {
                        BadRequest br = detail.unpack(
                            BadRequest.class);
                        for (BadRequest.FieldViolation fv
                                : br.getFieldViolationsList()) {
                            System.out.println("Field: "
                                + fv.getField()
                                + " – " + fv.getDescription());
                        }
                    } catch (Exception ex) {
                        ex.printStackTrace();
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
```

